.omo/
.codegraph
.freebuff/
AGENTS.md
.project_id
*.egg-info/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
artifacts/*
!artifacts/study-summaries/
# Local proof run (2026-09-13): the machine-checked rehearsal record - the
# verdict and session summary are durable evidence; the heavy checkpoint and
# dataset trees stay local scratch.
!artifacts/local-proof/
artifacts/local-proof/*
!artifacts/local-proof/verdict.json
!artifacts/local-proof/session-summary.json
# Real-data protocol proof (TinyStories through the section 5.1 machinery):
# the machine-checked verdict and session summary are durable evidence; the
# checkpoint/dataset scratch stays local.
!artifacts/real-proof/
artifacts/real-proof/*
!artifacts/real-proof/verdict.json
!artifacts/real-proof/session-summary.json
# Real-LM training record: the machine-checked report is durable evidence;
# the corpus (1.9 GB), token stream, and checkpoints stay local scratch.
!artifacts/real-lm/
artifacts/real-lm/*
!artifacts/real-lm/report.json
# The held-out stream the real-LM proof is scored on (2026-09-25). A perplexity
# with nothing beside it proves nothing - 5.5 could be good or terrible - so the
# record carries reference baselines, and those are recomputed from this file.
# 14 KB, versus a 1.9 GB corpus and a 250 MB checkpoint that stay local: it is
# the one piece that makes the proof checkable without either.
!artifacts/real-lm/val-tokens.npy
# Architecture-search record (2026-09-17). Every file here is load-bearing:
# the per-seed ledgers are the primary data (regenerating them costs GPU
# hours), `zoo_definition.json` is needed by scripts/arch_zoo_analyze.py to
# join structural axes onto old ledgers, and tests pin the phase's headline
# result by reading those ledgers. Only the progress logs are scratch.
!artifacts/ARCH_SEARCH_FINDINGS.md
!artifacts/arch-zoo/
artifacts/arch-zoo/*
!artifacts/arch-zoo/PERFORMANCE_NOTES.md
!artifacts/arch-zoo/SCREENING_AUDIT.md
!artifacts/arch-zoo/analysis.md
!artifacts/arch-zoo/zoo_definition.json
!artifacts/arch-zoo/zoo_results.json
# One block per family, not per experiment: the durable filenames are the same in
# every arch-zoo arm, and a new arm that needs a .gitignore edit before its
# evidence is committable is a new arm whose evidence gets silently dropped.
!artifacts/arch-zoo-*/
artifacts/arch-zoo-*/*
!artifacts/arch-zoo-*/NOTES.md
!artifacts/arch-zoo-*/decision.md
!artifacts/arch-zoo-*/ranked.json
!artifacts/arch-zoo-*/search_cost.json
!artifacts/arch-zoo-*/matching_report.json
!artifacts/arch-zoo-*/distance_matrix.json
!artifacts/arch-zoo-*/zoo_definition.json
!artifacts/arch-zoo-*/*_seed*_results.jsonl
!artifacts/mixer-benchmark/
artifacts/mixer-benchmark/*
!artifacts/mixer-benchmark/FINDINGS.md
!artifacts/mixer-benchmark/mixer_throughput.json
# Campaign session logs (2026-09-22): the platform's own log for a session that ran to
# completion, which is the only measurement anywhere of what the exit publish costs
# (25.42 GiB in 12 min) and of the child-output buffering that starved four failure
# captures. A log is evidence for a number here, so the filename pattern is stable -
# `session-<first>-<last>-log.json` - for the same reason the arch-zoo arm files are.
!artifacts/v0-session-logs/
artifacts/v0-session-logs/*
!artifacts/v0-session-logs/NOTES.md
!artifacts/v0-session-logs/session-*-log.json
# The two-seed concurrency rehearsal (2026-09-22): the blocker on the null queue's
# two-seeds-per-pair amendment, which the journal prices at 8.49 GPU-h and which is also the
# bar-level route to a one-week block. The record is the evidence - it carries both
# scenarios' full result payloads, so the comparison can be re-run from the artifact alone -
# and the two checkpoint trees stay local scratch.
!artifacts/null-pair-rehearsal/
artifacts/null-pair-rehearsal/*
!artifacts/null-pair-rehearsal/rehearsal.json
# The section 5.14 clause-power reading (2026-09-20, extended 2026-09-22): the artifact is
# the record the journal names as where the reading lives, and
# `tests/test_null_clause_power.py` asserts the committed file equals a fresh
# `build_report()`. It was left ignored by the blanket `artifacts/*` rule rather than by
# any decision, so the test could only pass on the machine that had generated it.
!artifacts/null-clause-power.json
# The raw depth-1 gate sweep behind the factor map (2026-09-12): report section 9.12
# cites it as the record showing the probe controller never ran in the legacy study,
# and `tests/test_factor_map_recheck.py` reads its first line to reproduce the
# published seed. It was left ignored by the blanket `artifacts/*` rule rather than by
# any decision, which is the same defect `null-clause-power.json` had - a test that
# could only pass on the machine that generated the file. 10 MB, and load-bearing:
# committing it is the option that keeps the report's citation true in a fresh clone.
!artifacts/gate3-384.jsonl
